ACME GLOBAL CORPORATION
Sustainability Report 2024
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW

Acme Global Corporation ("Acme") is a diversified industrial manufacturer
with operations in 23 countries and approximately 87,000 employees worldwide.
This report covers fiscal year 2024 performance against our sustainability commitments.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SECTION 1: GREENHOUSE GAS EMISSIONS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Scope 1 Emissions: 2.34 million metric tons CO2e (2024)
Scope 2 Emissions (market-based): 891,000 metric tons CO2e
Scope 2 Emissions (location-based): 1.12 million metric tons CO2e

Note: We do not currently report Scope 3 emissions but plan to begin
disclosure in 2025 with a focus on purchased goods and services (Category 1)
and use of sold products (Category 11).

GHG Intensity: 26.8 tCO2e per million USD revenue (down 8% from 2022 baseline)

We have committed to a 50% absolute reduction in Scope 1 and 2 emissions by 2035,
and net-zero across all scopes by 2050, aligned with the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi).

Methane Emissions: Our manufacturing operations released an estimated 4,200 metric tons
of methane in 2024, primarily from chemical processing. This represents a 12% reduction
from our 2020 baseline of 4,770 metric tons.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SECTION 2: ENERGY MANAGEMENT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Total Energy Consumption: 8.41 TWh (2024)
  Renewable electricity: 34.2% (2.88 TWh)
  Natural gas: 38.1% (3.20 TWh)
  Coal: 9.4% (0.79 TWh) — being phased out by 2028
  Other: 18.3%

Energy Intensity: 96.4 MWh per million USD revenue

In 2024 we signed a 200 MW virtual PPA for wind energy in Texas, expected to
go live in Q3 2025.

