SECTION 3: WATER AND WASTEWATER
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Total water withdrawn: 12.4 million cubic metres
Water withdrawn in high water stress regions: 22.8% (2.83 million m3)
Water recycled or reused: 31.4%

We are targeting a 25% reduction in water intensity by 2030 against a 2021 baseline.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SECTION 4: WASTE AND HAZARDOUS MATERIALS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Total waste generated: 187,400 metric tons
  Hazardous waste: 12,300 metric tons
  Recycled/recovered: 62.1%
  Landfilled: 19.3%
  Incinerated (energy recovery): 12.8%
  Other disposal: 5.8%

One significant reportable spill occurred in our Vietnam facility (Q2 2024),
involving 340 litres of hydraulic fluid. Remediation was completed within 48 hours.

